[TEXT] **ROOT CAUSE FOUND — Direct evidence on router6:**

Router6's iptables FORWARD chain has a blanket DROP ruleset for ALL traffic arriving on `eth2` (the WAN interface facing router3/10.50.1.x):
- Rule 1: ACCEPT only TCP:80 from 172.16.10.0/24 → 172.18.51.1
- Rule 2: DROP all TCP on eth2
- Rule 3: DROP all UDP on eth2 (9 pkts/540 bytes **already dropped**)
- Rule 4: DROP all ICMP on eth2 (49 pkts/4200 bytes **already dropped**)

